 task. Use this when you identify a task that matches a skill's description. ONLY use names exactly as they appear in the `<available_skills>` section.","kind":"other","parameterSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","enum":["skill-creator","k8s-deploy","gc-work","gc-rigs","gc-mail","gc-dispatch","gc-dashboard","gc-city","gc-agents"],"description":"The name of the skill to activate."}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"}},"invocation":{"params":"[Circular]"},"status":"success","response":{"callId":"hkcc25zn","responseParts":[{"functionResponse":{"id":"hkcc25zn","name":"activate_skill","response":{"output":"<activated_skill name=\"gc-work\">\n  <instructions>\n    # Work Items (Beads)\n\nEverything in Gas City is a bead — tasks, messages, molecules, convoys.\nThe `bd` CLI is the primary interface for bead CRUD.\n\n## Rig-scoped beads\n\nEach rig has its own `.beads/` database with its own ID prefix (e.g.\n`fe-` for frontend, `be-` for beads). **A bead must live in the\nsame database as the agent that will work on it.** When you sling a bead\nto a rig-scoped agent, sling operates on the agent's rig database — so\nthe bead must already exist there. The bead ID prefix tells you which\nrig it belongs to.\n\nUse `gc rig list` to see rig names, paths, and prefixes.\n\n## Creating work\n\n**Use `--rig` to create beads in the right database.** If the work will\nbe dispatched to a rig-scoped agent, create the bead in that agent's rig:\n\n```\nbd create \"title\" --rig frontend         # Create in frontend's db (fe- prefix)\nbd create \"title\" --rig beads            # Create in beads db (be- prefix)\nbd create \"title\"                        # Create in current directory's .beads/\nbd create \"title\" -t bug                 # Create with type\nbd create \"title\" --label priority=high  # Create with labels\n```\n\n## Finding work\n\n```\nbd list                                # List beads in current .beads/\nbd list --dir /path/to/rig             # List beads in a specific rig\nbd ready                               # List beads available for claiming\nbd ready --label role:worker           # Filter by label\nbd show <id>                           # Show bead details\n```\n\n## Claiming and updating\n\n```\nbd update <id> --claim                 # Claim a bead (sets assignee + in_progress)\nbd update <id> --status in_progress    # Update status\nbd update <id> --label <key>=<value>   # Add/update labels\nbd update <id> --note \"progress...\"    # Add a note\n```\n\n## Closing work\n\n```\nbd close <id>                          # Close a completed bead\nbd close <id> --reason \"done\"          # Close with reason\n```\n\n## Hooks\n\n```\ngc hook show <agent>                   # Show what's on an agent's hook\ngc agent claim <agent> <id>            # Put a bead on an agent's hook\n```\n  </instructions>\n\n  <available_resources>\n    Showing up to 200 items (files + folders).\n\n/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-work/\n└───SKILL.md\n  </available_resources>\n</activated_skill>"}}}],"resultDisplay":"Skill **gc-work** activated. Resources loaded from `/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-work`:\n\nShowing up to 200 items (files + folders).\n\n/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-work/\n└───SKILL.md","contentLength":2365},"durationMs":47,"outcome":"proceed_once","schedulerId":"root","approvalMode":"yolo"},{"request":{"callId":"yq15q6g9","name":"activate_skill","args":{"name":"gc-mail"},"isClientInitiated":false,"prompt_id":"a0b99eb0-49a6-4799-9de2-e221e01da386","traceId":"BB_0afHGC_2cz7IPhaGW2QU","schedulerId":"root"},"tool":{"name":"activate_skill","displayName":"Activate Skill","description":"Activates a specialized agent skill by name (Available: 'skill-creator', 'k8s-deploy', 'gc-work', 'gc-rigs', 'gc-mail', 'gc-dispatch