bead — tasks, messages, molecules, convoys.\nThe `bd` CLI is the primary interface for bead CRUD.\n\n## Rig-scoped beads\n\nEach rig has its own `.beads/` database with its own ID prefix (e.g.\n`fe-` for frontend, `be-` for beads). **A bead must live in the\nsame database as the agent that will work on it.** When you sling a bead\nto a rig-scoped agent, sling operates on the agent's rig database — so\nthe bead must already exist there. The bead ID prefix tells you which\nrig it belongs to.\n\nUse `gc rig list` to see rig names, paths, and prefixes.\n\n## Creating work\n\n**Use `--rig` to create beads in the right database.** If the work will\nbe dispatched to a rig-scoped agent, create the bead in that agent's rig:\n\n```\nbd create \"title\" --rig frontend         # Create in frontend's db (fe- prefix)\nbd create \"title\" --rig beads            # Create in beads db (be- prefix)\nbd create \"title\"                        # Create in current directory's .beads/\nbd create \"title\" -t bug                 # Create with type\nbd create \"title\" --label priority=high  # Create with labels\n```\n\n## Finding work\n\n```\nbd list                                # List beads in current .beads/\nbd list --dir /path/to/rig             # List beads in a specific rig\nbd ready                               # List beads available for claiming\nbd ready --label role:worker           # Filter by label\nbd show <id>                           # Show bead details\n```\n\n## Claiming and updating\n\n```\nbd update <id> --claim                 # Claim a bead (sets assignee + in_progress)\nbd update <id> --status in_progress    # Update status\nbd update <id> --label <key>=<value>   # Add/update labels\nbd update <id> --note \"progress...\"    # Add a note\n```\n\n## Closing work\n\n```\nbd close <id>                          # Close a completed bead\nbd close <id> --reason \"done\"          # Close with reason\n```\n\n## Hooks\n\n```\ngc hook show <agent>                   # Show what's on an agent's hook\ngc agent claim <agent> <id>            # Put a bead on an agent's hook\n```\n  </instructions>\n\n  <available_resources>\n    Showing up to 200 items (files + folders).\n\n/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-work/\n└───SKILL.md\n  </available_resources>\n</activated_skill>"}}}],"resultDisplay":"Skill **gc-work** activated. Resources loaded from `/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-work`:\n\nShowing up to 200 items (files + folders).\n\n/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-work/\n└───SKILL.md","contentLength":2365},"durationMs":47,"outcome":"proceed_once","schedulerId":"root","approvalMode":"yolo"},{"request":{"callId":"yq15q6g9","name":"activate_skill","args":{"name":"gc-mail"},"isClientInitiated":false,"prompt_id":"a0b99eb0-49a6-4799-9de2-e221e01da386","traceId":"BB_0afHGC_2cz7IPhaGW2QU","schedulerId":"root"},"tool":{"name":"activate_skill","displayName":"Activate Skill","description":"Activates a specialized agent skill by name (Available: 'skill-creator', 'k8s-deploy', 'gc-work', 'gc-rigs', 'gc-mail', 'gc-dispatch', 'gc-dashboard', 'gc-city', 'gc-agents'). Returns the skill's instructions wrapped in `<activated_skill>` tags. These provide specialized guidance for the current task. Use this when you identify a task that matches a skill's description. ONLY use names exactly as they appear in the `<available_skills>` section.","kind":"other","parameterSchema":"[Circular]"},"invocation":{"params":"[Circular]"},"status":"success","response":{"callId":"yq15q6g9","responseParts":[{"functionResponse":{"id":"yq15q6g9","name":"activate_skill","response":{"output":"<activated_skill name=\"gc-mail\">\n  <instructions>\n    # Messaging (Mail)\n\nMail is bead-based messaging between agents. Messages are beads with\ntype=message, stored in the bead store.\n\n## Sending\n\n```\ngc mail send <to> -m \"message body\"                    # Send a message\ngc mail send <to> -s \"Subject\" -m \"message body\"       # Send with subject\ngc mail reply <id> -m \"reply body\"                     # Reply to a message\ngc mail reply <id> -s \"Re: topic\" -m \"reply body\"      # Reply with subject\n```\n\n## Reading\n\n```\ngc mail inbox                          # List unread messages\ngc mail count                          # Count unread messages\ngc mail peek <id>                      # Preview a message without marking read\ngc mail read <id>                      # Read a message (marks as read)\ngc mail thread <id>                    # Show full conversation thread\n```\n\n## Managing\n\n```\ngc mail archive <id>                   # Archive a message\ngc mail mark-read <id>                 # Mark as read without displaying\ngc mail mark-unread <id>              # Mark as unread\ngc mail delete <id>                    # Delete a message\ngc mail check                          # Check for new mail (used in hooks)\n```\n  </instructions>\n\n  <available_resources>\n    Showing up to 200 items (files + folders).\n\n/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-mail/\n└───SKILL.md\n  </available_resources>\n</activated_skill>"}}}],"resultDisplay":"Skill **gc-mail** activated. Resources loaded from `/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-mail`:\n\nShowing up to 200 items (files + folders).\n\n/usr/local/google/home/jkramberger/agentic-ipa/ipa-city/.gemini/skills/core.gc-mail/\n└───SKILL.md","contentLength":1447},"durationMs":41,"outcome":"proceed_once","schedulerId":"root","approvalMode":"yolo"},{"request":{"callId":"xxebmxip","name":"activate_skill","args":{"name":"gc-agents"},"isClientInitiated":false,"prompt_id":"a0b99eb0-49a6-4799-9de2-e221e01da386","traceId":"BB_0afHGC_2cz7IPhaGW2QU","schedulerId":"root"},"tool":{"name":"activate_skill","displayName":"Activate Skill","description":"Activates a specialized agent skill by name 